Jahshaka patch 0080: the VCT TOTAL volume is an RGBA16F float; the DIRECT volume
stays 8-bit sRGB. (PHOTON-M3, 2026-09-20. SOURCE + MEDIA: every tree re-runs
build-ogre.sh.)

WHAT IT CHANGES
  * VctLighting::createTextures / setAllowMultipleBounces / every UAV view of the
    light voxels (the aniso mip jobs, the bounce, the injection): the TOTAL
    (mLightVoxel[0..3] + mLightBounce) is PFG_RGBA16_FLOAT. mLightDirect (patch
    0076's D term) stays PFG_RGBA8_UNORM_SRGB: D is <= the ceiling by construction
    (VctLighting::update's auto multiplier).
  * The total's textures are no longer TextureFlags::Reinterpretable: the flag
    served the 8-bit store's UNORM UAV view over an sRGB texture; a float store's
    UAV view is its own format. And a reinterpretable texture is created as its
    format FAMILY (R16G16B16A16_UINT for 16F), on which the mip chain's linear
    blit is invalid (VUID-vkCmdBlitImage-filter-02001) -- found by the validation
    suite on the first gate. The direct volume keeps the flag with its 8-bit store.
  * getLightDirectTexture(): a read-only accessor so a host can MEASURE the direct
    volume (Scene::giVoxelStats does; it is how the numbers below were read).
  * The media's store encoding follows the FORMAT instead of being hard-coded:
    jahStoreLight() under the uav0_orig_pf_srgb property HlmsComputeJob derives
    from the bound texture, in the injection, the bounce and both anisotropic mip
    generators (nine write sites); jahStoreDirect() under uav1_orig_pf_srgb for
    the direct term. An 8-bit sRGB store keeps its encode; a float one is written
    linear (a format with no fixed range has no transfer function to apply, and
    toSRGB of a value above 1 followed by a UNORM write is the clip this removes).
    Every READ of the light voxels is a sampler read, hardware-decoded for _SRGB
    and linear for 16F, so no reader changes.

WHY (spikes/photon-m3/MEASUREMENTS.md, sections 2-7)
  The volume holds the fixed point of L = D + rho * G(L), whose magnitude is
  D / (1 - rho * f) and has no bound a fixed-range store can hold: measured 2.05x
  the direct term in a closed room of albedo 0.79, 2.76x and still climbing at
  albedo 1.0 (what every shipped sample's walls carry), 3.5x in World Background
  as it ships. The 8-bit store clips 3-26 % of the lit voxels of the three
  enclosed samples today, and shows 82 % of the white room's bounce light at four
  bounces with a series whose increments collapse (0.30, 0.39) where the physics
  says 0.65-0.70. A fixed headroom H does not fix it: the H a room needs is
  unbounded, and every H costs the dark end (H = 2 rounds 0.65 % of the directly
  lit voxels to black, H = 8 4.9 %) where the GI signal lives; the float store
  holds 3.8 % more energy than the best H arm.

COST (Showroom 2, 1080p, clocks locked, three ABAB rounds): the cone march reads
  4.36 ms against 4.44-4.46 ms on the 8-bit store at High and Epic (the sampler
  does no sRGB decode on a float volume), never more than 0.2 ms slower in any
  round; VRAM +36 MB at High, +56 MB at Epic. The selftest poses move by exactly
  one code on 1.4 % / 2.0 % of their pixels, brighter (the dark end no longer
  rounds to black).

